From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:18:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150: no reset for mdss

The mdss node's reset pointed at gcc with a dispcc index, so it named
GCC_EMAC_BCR (index 0 in gcc), and msm_mdss_init() held the Ethernet
MAC's block reset for 20 ms on every probe. The display subsystem was
never reset by it. Drop it, as upstream's sm8150.dtsi has none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
index 87579145918b..e85890923e63 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150.dtsi
@@ -3840,8 +3840,6 @@ mdss: display-subsystem@ae00000 {
 
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x800 0x420>;
 
-			resets = <&gcc DISP_CC_MDSS_CORE_BCR>;
-
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			#address-cells = <2>;
